{
 "case": "SRC-10",
 "says": "One person has two checkouts of repository W on their laptop: a clone on main at /home/ana/work and a worktree on a feature branch at /home/ana/work-feature-backups; each observation's selection names its own checkout. Each is observed and bound with repository.bind; both bindings name the same repository id W, each with the working_bytes_digest of its own observation. The ADR directory of W is registered as a memory source, a workstream is opened, and memory.record.publish records the journal-mode choice from 0001-journal-mode.md as that source's first revision. A fork of W is observed and bound with its own repository id, naming W as the ancestor it derives new authority from and the clone's binding as its authority evidence, not as an explicit binding to read W through it. Resolving the ADR source from the fork as if it were W is refused with repository_binding_required, and registering a second home for the same source in the fork (a copied manifest taking over as another writer) is refused with source_home_conflict; neither writes anything. Then the clone switches to a branch where 0001-journal-mode.md is absent; a new observation no longer lists it, and rebinding the same repository id now observes branch chore/prune-old-adrs in place of main, still sharing W's identity and this later observation's working_bytes_digest. memory.state.resolve for the workstream still reports the choice as current from the ADR source at the head it was published at: a file missing from a checkout or a branch switch is not a withdrawal.",
